WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
<i>Naha Airbase</i>

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.950
Let's make it clear who's right.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.080
If we win, you're going to 
change the way you act.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.820
You're the new girl, and you're 
going to start listening to orders.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:18.160
And if I win, you'll do whatever I tell you?

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.280
Hm...

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:25.300
Then I'll ask you to leave Gripen 
and be my partner instead, maybe.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.370
Very well.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.260
Are you certain?

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.460
You don't even have the 
slightest chance of winning.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.430
Gripen is an incomplete Anima.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.010
You can't win against me in a fair fight,

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.420
or even if you try to trick me somehow.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.060
Do you still really intend to fight?

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.570
I'll ask you the same question.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:50.530
That way, when we kick your ass,
you won't be able to make excuses.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:28.500
<i>After the Bewilderment</i>

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.240
<i>So, um... sorry.</i>

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.570
<i>We're going to have a real fight.</i>

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.070
"Impossible. What the 
hell are you thinking?"

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.580
...is what I'd like to say.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.160
But words wouldn't be enough to persuade her.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.710
<i>I'm surprised.</i>

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:41.880
<i>I thought you'd be mad.</i>

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.860
We don't have time for a lengthy debate.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.870
If Phantom doesn't participate 
in tomorrow's operation,

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:49.790
we're not going to succeed.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.270
And that would mean that Japan falls to the Xi.

00:02:56.270 --> 00:03:00.310
<i>But we don't have time for a mock battle.</i>

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.310
<i>Eagle and Gripen's Daughters need repairs.</i>

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.410
<i>What are you going to do?</i>

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.270
We'll borrow the base's simulators.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:14.160
<i>But even if Phantom agreed to the fight,
 do you have a way to win?</i>

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.930
<i>She'll crack your systems in a simulator 
just like she would in the sky.</i>

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:21.250
<i>She's the type who'll do 
whatever it takes to win.</i>

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.570
That's why we'll do the same thing.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.020
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.460
I mean...

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.860
<i>That's basically gambling!</i>

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:34.980
I know it's risky.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.850
But is there any other way?

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:39.350
Fine. I'll help.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.100
I'll send Funato.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.820
If he leaves now, he'll make it by evening.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:48.220
Our second try at the operation 
is at 0620, before dawn tomorrow.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.580
We're launching the attack regardless 
of whether Phantom participates.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:55.300
<i>Not that there's any way to know how many of 
those cruise missiles will hit without her.</i>

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:58.030
I don't really want to think about it.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:59.460
<i>I'm counting on you.</i>

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:02.300
<i>Bring that tomboy back in line.</i>

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:05.010
<i>Feel free to get a little rough 
with her if you have to.</i>

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.030
As long as her father approves.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:07.960
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.960
Now, I need to go talk to Gripen.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.510
What's wrong?

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.220
Are you not feeling well?

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.780
You don't want me anymore.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:29.600
You said you were willing 
to be Phantom's partner.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.960
That's only if we lose.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:34.290
But if we fight, 
we're probably going to lose.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:37.520
If you accepted her conditions when 
there's no way for us to win,

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.670
it means you don't want me anymore.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.590
I'm so stunned, I can't even stand.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.230
I'll never recover.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.210
I want to die.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.380
Listen, Gripen.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:50.870
We're going to win.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.270
We're going to persuade Phantom to help us,

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.790
destroy the Xi base, 
and all go back to Komatsu.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.770
That's why we're going to fight her.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:02.290
Of course, I'll never give you up.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:06.110
We're partners. We need each other.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.820
Don't make me say that after 
everything that's happened.

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:13.360
I'll explain how we're going to win.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:17.490
Kei, where are you right now?

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:18.560
<i>On base.</i>

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.180
<i>I said I had to work.</i>

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:21.330
Did you?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:25.230
Anyway, we ran into some 
trouble doing inventory,

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:27.050
and I might be staying here tonight.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.350
<i>Staying there?</i>

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:30.160
They don't have enough help.

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.140
I can't say no, it looks like.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:36.490
Fine. I'll bring you supper,

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:38.270
so wait outside the base for me.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.670
<i>Well...</i>

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:41.720
You can come out for a minute or so, right?

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:45.770
It'd be really hard to 
get out there in time.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.410
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.680
Um... Well...

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:50.960
It's Kei!

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:51.700
Hugs!

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:57.080
<i>Huh? "Hugs"? Kei,
I just heard a girl's voice.</i>

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.660
<i>Are you up to something?</i>

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:00.750
Sorry, I'll call you back!

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:02.910
Eagle!

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.630
Daddy told me!

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.170
He said you're trying to avenge me!

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:09.240
Huh?

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:13.770
He said you'd kick Phantom's butt 
and make her apologize to me!

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.930
He said you love me and you were mad

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:19.130
that she was mean to the girl you loved!

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.820
I love Daddy best,

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:25.640
so we can't be together,
 but you made me really happy!

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.360
<i>Why did he tell her that?</i>

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.560
This hug is my thank you!

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.560
Couldn't you have picked a better time?

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:33.530
Anyway, get off me. Okay?

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:36.210
Do you not like hugs?

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:39.650
I do, but... That's not the issue here.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:43.380
Aren't you nervous about tomorrow?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.160
Nope.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.080
You're not...

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:50.140
If you had to pick between Japan and the
 whole world, which would you protect?

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:54.900
Let's say that if we lose the 
battle tomorrow, Japan is doomed,

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:57.320
but if you go out there, 
there's no hope of surviving.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:00.150
If you want to save all of humanity,

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:02.480
it's better not to fight tomorrow at all.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:03.660
What would you do?

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:08.990
I can just come back 
alive and keep fighting.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:11.970
Go out there like "whoosh," 
and then win like "boom"!

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.150
Is that weird?

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:17.580
No, I just feel a whole lot more relaxed now.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:20.160
Each of you girls really 
are unique, aren't you?

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:24.800
You each have your own personality 
and other things that make you unique.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:27.840
So there must be a place where 
all of your values meet.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.390
Getting there is our first goal.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.700
We can figure out the rest later.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.260
What are you talking about?

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.990
I'm saying that someday, we'll all 
be able to understand each other.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.890
Thank you, Eagle.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.690
That was a much better present than a hug.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:47.370
I don't get it.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.550
Oh, there you are.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:01.500
Hey.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:06.040
I did what the director asked me to.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.750
Sorry. I know it's sudden.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.300
It's fine.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.010
I'm not sure I approve,

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:15.890
but knowing you, I'm sure you've got a plan.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:17.750
Thank you.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.850
Oh, you're having a strategy meeting.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.820
Would you like me to wait?

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:25.470
What are you talking about?

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:26.690
We don't have a strategy.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:31.310
We're going to defeat you 
head on, in a fair fight.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:35.420
And there's no reason you brought your 
favorite engineer all the way from Komatsu?

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:38.460
Funa-san came to repair the Daughters.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.240
He's only tuning up the 
simulators while he's here.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:43.250
Come on, there's no time to waste.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.220
Let's get started.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:55.430
To confirm, it's really okay to decide 
my participation in this operation

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:58.040
based on the outcome of the battle?

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:01.380
Yeah. I've gotten Yashirodoori-san's approval.

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:06.010
Don't do anything lame, like sobbing 
and begging, after you lose.

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:07.290
You, too.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:09.740
When you start crying and begging 
for forgiveness, it will be too late.

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:13.690
Okay, let's get started.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.890
The combat area will be the 
vicinity of Naha Airport.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:23.130
This is a one-on-one dogfight.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.590
Everybody, review the mission parameters.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:27.000
The weather is cloudy.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.540
Cloud cover is 7/8.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:31.180
<i>Wind direction is 180 degrees,
 speed is 5 knots.</i>

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.770
Well? How are you feeling?

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.010
Not bad.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.930
It's better-made than the one at Komatsu.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.260
I can fly it without issue.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:41.620
Good.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.150
<i>Let's see what you've got.</i>

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:48.760
<i>Also, do note that I 
neutralized the processing</i>

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:52.040
<i>delay program you put into my simulator.</i>

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:56.340
It would have delayed my control response 
by several fractions of a second.

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:58.900
Did you have Funato-san put that in?

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:01.800
<i>I'm impressed you managed to do 
it in such a short span of time,</i>

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.160
<i>but it was a rather rough piece of work.</i>

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:07.910
I ran 120 or so test signals through 
it and found it immediately.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:13.140
<i>Don't worry. I've done nothing to your unit.</i>

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:17.000
<i>So far, that is. I can't say what 
I'll do when the battle begins.</i>

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.310
<i>Good luck.</i>

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:22.890
<i>No way... That's way too fast.</i>

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:26.050
Okay, break left and right,
 and begin the mission.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:28.720
The dogfight begins when 
you intersect again.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.000
Three,

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:31.490
two,

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:33.070
<i>one...</i>

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:39.300
Gripen, does anything feel wrong?

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:40.450
I don't know.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:44.860
I don't even know if she's using 
the same signals as last time.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:47.910
So we may already be under attack?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:48.740
Yeah.

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.280
Can we rely on our radar?

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.830
What do we do, Kei?

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:55.950
Fight normally, for now.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:58.240
I'll keep an eye on things.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:10:59.350
Roger.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:02.360
<i>She's in the clouds, huh?</i>

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.250
Target lock on.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.400
Fox...

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:10.230
What?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.130
Damn it!

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:16.990
That position is totally 
different than before!

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:20.670
Did she really move?

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:22.250
Or is it a fakeout?

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:26.440
Radar says left.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.180
Thermal says below...

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:30.870
But I'm being locked on from behind...

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:33.050
Kei, I'm sorry.

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:34.740
I can't keep this up.

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:36.880
Gripen!

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:39.750
Looks like you tried a lot of things...

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:41.690
But you're right there!

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:46.830
Fox 2!

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:54.570
Barbie 03 is down!

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:56.580
Gripen wins!

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:04.740
What did you do?

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:07.820
I took out your radar and data link.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.770
How did you find me?

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:13.050
You were doing a bad job of concealing 
your intent to kill, maybe.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.460
Don't make that face.

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:20.460
These simulators are multiseat, right?

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:23.330
You can put a different system in each seat.

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:26.460
We put in an Anima system for the front seat,

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:29.480
and a human system in the rear.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:31.300
And what did that do?

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:34.520
You took over the Anima data link, right?

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.570
So...

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:36.940
Kei, I'm sorry.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.810
I can't keep this up.

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:42.620
I cut off the information 
coming in from her,

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:45.270
and made it so I could receive 
information from the craft directly.

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:50.200
Once we were just an ordinary manned fighter,
 it was easy to spot you.

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:55.540
But how could she fly like 
that when she was dazed?

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:58.000
Who said Gripen was piloting?

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:02.540
Halfway through, all she was 
doing was sitting there.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:05.210
At the end, I was the one flying.

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:07.010
A human pilot?

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:10.880
An Anima and a human taking turns 
piloting a Daughter?

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:15.020
Even a veteran like you doesn't
 know everything yet, right?

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:19.470
That delay program was a decoy.

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:24.480
To hide the fact that we'd isolated my 
interface and switched control over to me.

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:26.630
You let your guard down after 
making your first discovery,

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:29.290
and had no idea you walked into a trap.

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:32.900
Well? This is a new 
experience for you, right?

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:41.040
Very well.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:45.050
If you're going to tell me to participate 
in tomorrow's mission, I'll accept.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:49.350
But I do have one condition.

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:50.430
Condition?

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:54.850
I want you to pilot the Daughter 
during the next mission, Kei-san.

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:56.230
Me?

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.310
No! Don't!

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:11.080
Mom!

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:28.850
<i>I want you to pilot the Daughter 
during the next mission, Kei-san.</i>

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:33.010
Gripen's current combat 
abilities are very low.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.900
To tell the truth, she lacks
the capacity to handle piloting,

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:38.700
radar control, and weapons
systems simultaneously.

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:41.690
She knows that better than anybody.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:46.810
So the best option is to split 
things up with a co-pilot.

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:48.010
Split them up?

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:52.900
Gripen's maneuvers are capped at 
9Gs in order to keep you safe.

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:56.840
So a human pilot won't perform 
all that differently than her.

00:14:57.320 --> 00:15:00.820
Instead, the Anima can handle 
the radar and weapons systems,

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:03.350
boosting sensors and lock-on capability.

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:06.220
And how do we handle the HiMAT?

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:10.670
The strength of an Anima is that it can 
handle the Xi's maneuverability, right?

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:14.740
Only idiots do repeated 
high-speed maneuvers.

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.640
What's important is altitude and speed.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:22.570
You must minimize loss of kinetic energy and 
ensure you're always in the optimum position.

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:23.810
That's all.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:28.740
Don't worry. I'll be there to help you.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:31.870
You want me to fight the Xi?

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.670
Am I going to fight them?

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:04.490
<i>I'm going to pilot Gripen?</i>

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:05.930
Kei?

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.740
Gripen!

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.130
What's wrong?

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:11.240
I thought you'd be asleep.

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:17.110
I couldn't get any rest.

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:18.640
You couldn't?

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:20.670
Do you promise not to laugh?

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.120
It's pretty pathetic,

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.540
but when I think about 
piloting in a dogfight,

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:28.730
I can't stop shaking.

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:32.290
To tell the truth, I'm so scared.

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:36.060
You're strong.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.730
You don't complain even when 
you have trouble flying.

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:41.040
You keep trying, never giving up.

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:42.860
That's wrong.

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:45.130
I'm not strong.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:48.450
But there are a lot of people 
in the world who can't fight.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:51.460
Who can't shoot down the Xi.

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:55.770
Compared to them, I'm blessed.

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:59.070
I can struggle against 
them with my own power.

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:00.530
I can fight.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:03.450
Complaining is a luxury.

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:04.980
Yeah.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.580
A normal person can't even 
die while putting up a fight.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:12.680
But now I have the power to defeat the Xi.

00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:15.620
I have wings that can fight back.

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:18.460
That's a real luxury.

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:19.930
Luxury is the enemy.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:23.860
No, I know what you're trying to say, but...

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.470
I feel a little better.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:27.560
Okay.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:30.470
Wait, aren't you going to rest?

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:32.810
You should get some sleep while you can.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:35.750
I need to tune my Daughter.

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:37.060
But I'm fine.

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:38.910
I took a nap.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:39.870
And...

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:40.660
And?

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:44.140
I was able to talk with 
you because I was awake.

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:48.080
I was able to learn about your fears.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.120
Gripen?

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:51.460
Don't worry.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:56.100
No matter what happens, I'll be there 
to back you up until the very end.

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:59.080
I won't let you fly alone.

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:02.160
So... let's fight together, Kei.

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:03.870
Y-Yeah.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:07.020
Anyway, I'm heading back to the barracks.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.210
Get some rest, too.

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:11.980
What's that?

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:14.080
The Viper Zero.

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.400
Naha Base's Daughter.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.900
Viper Zero?

00:18:18.230 --> 00:18:20.390
The F-2A-ANM.

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:25.240
A combat fighter based on the 
American F16-C Fighting Falcon.

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:30.370
But the upgrades to it were so great that it 
bears little resemblance to its base model.

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:34.930
It's a pervert, a 40-year old design 
loaded with the latest instruments.

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:36.640
Pervert?

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:40.980
A fighter than can carry 
four AShMs is a pervert.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:43.080
If it's that amazing,

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:46.390
why didn't it participate 
in the last mission?

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:48.740
Naha Base is on the front lines of the war.

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:52.270
Protecting it is Viper Zero's job.

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:55.440
So it never participates in other missions.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:59.920
So when it does participate, 
it means things are really bad, huh?

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.030
Yes.

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.990
What game are you two playing?

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:06.400
Let me join in!

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:07.540
Get off me!

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.330
Let me join in!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.860
We're not playing! Let go!

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:17.590
<i>The Taiwanese Air Force, the US Air Force,</i>

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:20.870
<i>and the forces at Naha will 
be launching a decoy.</i>

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:24.670
<i>The hope is that they can lure out the 
planes buzzing around Umidori Island.</i>

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:27.000
This is a pretty large-scale operation.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.570
<i>The bosses have a fire 
lit under their asses now.</i>

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:33.330
<i>Air routes over the East China Sea
 have been totally cut off.</i>

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:37.310
<i>Supply lines to the front will 
collapse if they don't act fast.</i>

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:39.810
<i>Well, it's a bigger deal now,</i>

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:42.650
<i>but that doesn't change the fact 
that we're counting on you.</i>

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:43.970
<i>Good luck out there.</i>

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:49.170
So the three of us end up 
charging in alone, huh?

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:52.540
Well, that was always the plan.

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:54.570
<i>Skipper Head to Barbie.</i>

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:55.550
<i>We have an emergency.</i>

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:59.990
<i>The Taiwanese unit has been wiped 
out by another enemy unit.</i>

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:02.880
<i>A new Xi force is heading for the 7th Fleet.</i>

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:05.450
Barbie 01 to Skipper Head.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:06.840
Is anyone going to defend the fleet?

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:08.990
<i>A unit is heading from Naha Base,</i>

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:10.760
<i>but it'll take time to arrive.</i>

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.930
Are we closer?

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:14.130
<i>No.</i>

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:19.170
If we go to support them, we'll use up
all of our ammunition and fuel.

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.620
Let's continue on our way.

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:24.120
But there's no point if the fleet sinks.

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:26.030
Let's split up.

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:29.220
One of us will go to support the fleet.

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:31.870
The other two will continue the mission.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:34.130
You want us to attack the 
island with just two of us?

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:34.770
That's crazy.

00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:38.790
Crazy or not, we have to 
use the forces we've got.

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:40.140
We don't have the luxury of asking for more.

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:42.330
Luxury is the enemy.

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:44.220
Fine.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:47.270
I'll go drive off as many of them as I can.

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:50.300
We'll just have to hang in there 
until reinforcements arrive.

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:52.360
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:55.260
<i>Please protect me, per our original plan.</i>

00:20:56.050 --> 00:20:58.680
Eagle, go protect the fleet.

00:20:58.680 --> 00:21:01.810
Why are you telling me what to do?

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:03.820
This isn't coming from me.

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:08.020
Father told me that this was the 
plan if something happened.

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:09.270
R-Really?

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:10.150
Really.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:16.840
He said that the enemy would stand no chance 
in the face of your unstoppable onslaught.

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:19.660
Though I'm reluctant to say it, I agree.

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:22.250
Then that's different!

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:26.010
Daddy said he was counting on me.

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:28.850
Okay, I'll go shoot down all the bad guys!

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:31.690
Was that...

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:32.960
<i>It was a lie.</i>

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:34.190
Thought so.

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:39.140
<i>Can Gripen and I actually protect Phantom?</i>

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:41.360
Kei, radar contact.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:42.220
Head on.

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:54.320
There they are!

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:30.250
Next time on <i>Girly Air Force</i>...

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:34.010
ALT 08: "An Unhappy Top Secret."

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>An Unhappy Top Secret</i>

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:38.230
Barbie 01, cleared for take off!
